TY  - JOUR
TI  - CLIPDraw: Exploring Text-to-Drawing Synthesis through Language-Image Encoders
AU  - Kevin Frans
AU  - Lisa Soros
AU  - Olaf Witkowski
PY  - 2022
AB  - CLIPDraw is an algorithm that synthesizes novel drawings from natural language input. It does not require any additional training; rather, a pre-trained CLIP language-image encoder is used as a metric for maximizing similarity between the given description and a generated drawing. Crucially, CLIPDraw operates over vector strokes rather than pixel images, which biases drawings towards simpler human-recognizable shapes. Results compare CLIPDraw with other synthesis-through-optimization methods, as well as highlight various interesting behaviors of CLIPDraw.
UR  - https://papers.nips.cc/paper_files/paper/2022/hash/21f76686538a5f06dc431efea5f475f5-Abstract-Conference.html
